<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#old-french">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old French</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Old French is the form of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-language">French language</a> spoken from around the ninth to the fourteenth century. It developed from the spoken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> of the western Frankish lands. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaths-of-strasbourg">Oaths of Strasbourg</a> of 842 CE, sworn by Carolingian rulers, are regarded as the earliest surviving text in a recognisable form of the language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-french.jpg" alt="Old French" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Renart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
